     "SONAR Source-Available License v1.0" (not GPL-compatible if it were distributed; it is an analyzer
     used while compiling and is not part of the output).
   - libe_sqlite3.so (SQLite) is produced by the SDK build but not shipped by the packages.

2. Proton cryptography (libproton_crypto.so)
   - Source: https://github.com/ProtonDriveApps/dotnet-crypto, revision pinned in
     scripts/build-native.sh (Rust FFI crate proton-crypto-ffi)
   - Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Proton AG
   - Licence text: LICENSE.txt of that repository; shipped in the native archive as
     LICENSE-proton-dotnet-crypto.txt and in third_party/dotnet-crypto/LICENSE.txt.
   - Statically linked Rust crates (178 third-party crates; the FFI crate itself, which has no licence
     field, is not listed and is covered by the MIT licence of the repository): licenses/rust-proton-crypto.tsv.
     Retained licences: MIT 169, BSD-3-Clause 5, Zlib 1 (zlib-rs), Unicode-3.0 1, Apache-2.0 1
     (self_cell, "Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-only"), bzip2-1.0.6 1 (libbz2-rs-sys, permissive).
     Their licence files are in the sources of each crate, not in the native archive.

