4. Other Rust crates of the PDrive programs (pdrive, pdrived, pdrive-app)
   - Vendored in the source archive pdrive-for-linux-<version>.tar.xz under vendor/, each
     with its own licence files; THIRD_PARTY_CRATES.txt in that archive lists name, version and
     declared licence expression.
   - Audited inventory (Linux target, without dev-dependencies): licenses/rust-pdrive.tsv, 381
     third-party crates. Retained licence (an accepted alternative of each expression): MIT 337,
     Unicode-3.0 19, Apache-2.0 10, BSD-3-Clause 5, ISC 3, Zlib 1, Unlicense 1, CDLA-Permissive-2.0 1
     (webpki-roots, data licence), plus the four Proton crates of item 3 (MIT). Some crates offer
