     GPL-3.0-compatible permissive licences; MIT, BSD and Apache-2.0 require their notices to be kept in
     binary distributions. `scripts/audit-licenses.sh --texts <file>` writes the texts delivered by
     the crates (grouped, with the crates using each) for that purpose.
   - The Proton crates (proton-crypto, proton-crypto-account, proton-rpgp, proton-srp) declare no
     `license` field in Cargo.toml; their LICENSE file is the MIT licence, "Copyright (c) 2025 Proton AG".

5. System libraries
   - GTK 4, libadwaita, GLib/GIO, libnautilus-extension, FUSE (fusermount3), glibc and
     libgcc are not bundled: they are used from the distribution (dependencies of the
     package) under their own licences.

The licence files of the sources above are in third_party/ after scripts/build-native.sh
and in the native archive. The audit is automated and factual: a human must review it before any public distribution.
